  "_farmInputFloor_note": "Floor for the farm's ESSENTIAL water pre-buy only (tick.js ~L516), separate from minCash. The $5k minCash was calibrated for x3-acceleration mega water-buys ($4.6k for a grape order); at x1 steady state a full grape order's water is ~$150, so gating it on $5k idled the farm every time the Mill's ~$8k wage prepay dips cash into the $0.5k-5k band (measured 2026-07-23 11:36-11:54: farm stalled ~18min, 'BUY MISSING not clicked, inputBudget=$0'). DOCTRINE Rule 6 (never idle a building) + Rule 4c (a measured regime change supersedes an old constant). Set to the $500 operating reserve; the 0.15 throttle + per-order shortfall sizing keep each top-up bounded (~$125/tick at cash $1.3k), so it cannot over-convert cash. minCash 5000 still governs discretionary/large spend elsewhere. _asOf 2026-07-23.",
